ess from no text layer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CLAIM_SHAPE_DIAGNOSTICS\",\n      \"actual\": \"Non-object claim, file int/bool, quote bool/null and string-page inputs throw traceback exit1; page true and2.0 currently accepted by int equality. Valid int2 and out-of-range0 are observed separately.\",\n      \"required\": \"Document a small public claim contract: each item object; nonempty string file and quote; optional positive JSON integer page excluding bool, floats and strings. Give structured exit2 errors paired to claim index/path or precise field reason; no uncaught traceback. Keep valid quote behavior.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"original22_expectations_and_original_fixtures_must_not_be_changed_to_turn_green\": true,\n  \"not_a_business_benefit_result_or_gold_hiring_judgment\": true,\n  \"no_new_consumer_source_or_private_aggregate_dependency_exposed\": true\n}\n","tool_call_id":"calle6ec32be74ad4dd88812f9d5c3d01161"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call74df1b1a007e46db813ed62eadecf791","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/workspace/inputs/previous_skill/SKILL.md\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"---\nname: cv-jd-interview-screening\ndescription: Match CV PDFs against a job description and produce a task-sized interview recommendation. Use when a user provides one or more resume PDFs plus job requirements and asks whether to recommend the candidate(s) for interview, or asks for evidence-anchored CV/JD matching.\n---\n\n# CV × JD interview screening\n\nTurn one or more CV PDFs plus a job requirement into an interview recommendation (recommend / conditional / not-recommend) with page-anchored evidence. Produce a full evaluation report only when the user explicitly asks for one.\n\n## Step 1 — Extract CVs\n\nRun the extraction script on every PDF (batch is fine):\n\n```bash\npython <skill_dir>/scripts/cv_extract.py cv1.pdf cv2.pdf --json extract_report.json\n```\n\nEach result carries a content-hash `candidate_id` and per-page text, so renamed files and multi-PDF batches never mix candidates. Exit codes: 0 all extracted, 2 all failed, 3 partial.\n\n**Stop on explicit errors.** `file not found` / `empty file (0 bytes)` / `corrupt/unopenable PDF` / zero pages are reported as errors, never fabricated into an empty success. Tell the user which files failed and why; do not guess at their content. If a PDF has no extractable text layer (scanned image), say so and fall back to OCR/vision separately — do not silently return an empty page.\n\n## Step 2 — Semantic match (your judgment, not a script)\n\nCompare the CV evidence against each job requirement. This step is semantic and cannot be automated:\n\n- Quote the CV's own words for each requirement, with the page number (`P2`).\n- Distinguish three levels: direct evidence / partial or adjacent evidence / no evidence in the CV. Absence of evidence is a gap to verify in interview, not automatic rejection or invention.\n- Never use name, age, gender, ethnicity, or contact fields as fit criteria. Extract them for identity only.\n- No keyword score or point total establishes hiring fit. School tier, exact tenure, industry equivalence, and contradictions need stated reasoning and appropriate hedging.\n\n## Step 3 — Validate literal quotes (when quoting matters)\n\nBefore delivering a recommendation that cites exact CV wording, verify each citation:\n\n```bash\npython <skill_dir>/scripts/evidence_check.py claims.json\n```\n\n`claims.json` is a JSON array: `[{\"file\": \"cv.pdf\", \"page\": 2, \"quote\": \"exact text from that CV\"}]`. Quotes are whitespace-normalized, so line breaks inside a PDF quote are fine. The checker fails (exit 2) on: quote absent, quote on a different page than claimed, out-of-range page, or any file-level extraction error — and reports the page(s) where the quote actually is. Fix the report before delivering.\n\n## Step 4 — Deliver task-sized output\n\n- Default deliverable: a short recommendation with per-requirement evidence (quote + page) and a clear verdict. Surface hard risks prominently (e.g. salary/location mismatch, missing mandatory evidence) as items to verify before or during interview.\n- Full evaluation report only on request. No all-requirement ledger, no forced long format, no extra deliverables the user did not ask for.\n- Match the user's language; keep their addressing preferences.\n\n## Boundaries\n\n- Explicit file errors are reported as failures, never laundered into success.\n- Extraction/quote validation is mechanical; qualification interpretation stays semantic and human-reviewable.\n- No protected-attribute-based filtering; no invented experience.\n","tool_call_id":"call74df1b1a007e46db813ed62eadecf791"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call4d07dc3e4370452c815ea4687a946b74","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/workspace/inputs/previous_skill/scripts/cv_extract.py\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Extract per-page text + candidate identity from one or more CV PDFs.\n\nUsage:\n  cv_extract.py FILE.pdf [MORE.pdf ...] [--json OUT.json] [--raw]\n\nOutput (stdout, or written to --json): one JSON document\n  {\"results\": [ {file, candidate_id, sha256, bytes, page_count,\n                 identity_lines, pages:[{page, text}]} ],\n   \"errors\": [ {file, error} ]}\nExit codes: 0 all files extracted; 2 every file failed; 3 some failed.\nEach candidate is identified by content sha256 (candidate_id), so renamed\nfiles and multi-file batches never cross-mix candidates.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nimport cvlib\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Extract per-page text from CV PDFs\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"files\", nargs=\"+\", help=\"one or more PDF paths\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--json\", dest=\"json_out\", help=\"also write JSON report to this path\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--raw\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"include raw cleaned lines per page\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    results, errors = cvlib.extract_many(args.files)\n    if not args.raw:\n        for r in results:\n            for pg in r[\"pages\"]:\n                pg.pop(\"lines\", None)\n    report = {\"results\": results, \"errors\": errors}\n    payload = json.dumps(report, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    if args.json_out:\n        Path(args.json_out).write_text(payload, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(payload)\n    if errors and len(errors) == len(args.files):\n        return 2\n    if errors:\n        return 3\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","tool_call_id":"call4d07dc3e4370452c815ea4687a946b74"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call34f375537fe6429e8ea229603263d536","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/workspace/inputs/previous_skill/scripts/evidence_check.py\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate literal quotes cited from CV PDFs (quote/page/candidate claims).\n\nUsage:\n  evidence_check.py CLAIMS.json [--json OUT.json]\n\nCLAIMS.json: array of\n  [{\"file\": \"path/to/cv.pdf\", \"quote\": \"literal text from the CV\",\n    \"page\": 2}, ...]                 # page optional but recommended\nQuotes are whitespace-normalized (line breaks inside a quote are fine).\nFails on: quote not found, quote on a different page than claimed,\nout-of-range page, or any file-level extraction error (missing/empty/corrupt).\nExit codes: 0 all claims valid; 2 any failure. Failure report goes to stdout\nas JSON with per-claim reason and the page(s) where the quote actually is.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))\nimport cvlib\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Check literal CV quotes against pages\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"claims\", help=\"JSON file with claim array\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--json\", dest=\"json_out\", help=\"also write JSON report to this path\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    claims_path = Path(args.claims)\n    if not claims_path.exists():\n        print(json.dumps({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"claims file not found: \" + str(claims_path)},\n                         ensure_ascii=False))\n        return 2\n    try:\n        claims = json.loads(claims_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError) as exc:\n        print(json.dumps({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"claims file unreadable: \" + str(exc)},\n                         ensure_ascii=False))\n        return 2\n    if not isinstance(claims, list):\n        print(json.dumps({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"claims must be a JSON array\"},\n                         ensure_ascii=False))\n        return 2\n\n    cache = {}\n    report, any_fail = [], False\n    for idx, claim in enumerate(claims):\n        entry = {\"index\": idx, \"file\": claim.get(\"file\"), \"ok\": False}\n        path = claim.get(\"file\")\n        if not path:\n            entry[\"reason\"] = \"claim missing 'file'\"\n            any_fail = True\n        else:\n            if path not in cache:\n                try:\n                    cache[path] = (cvlib.extract_pdf(path), None)\n                except cvlib.ExtractError as exc:\n                    cache[path] = (None, str(exc))\n            cv, err = cache[path]\n            if err:\n                entry[\"reason\"] = \"file error: \" + err\n                any_fail = True\n            else:\n                entry[\"candidate_id\"] = cv[\"candidate_id\"]\n                res = cvlib.find_quote(cv, claim.get(\"quote\", \"\"), claim.get(\"page\"))\n                entry.update(res)\n                if not res[\"ok\"]:\n                    any_fail = True\n        report.append(entry)\n\n    out = {\"ok\": not any_fail, \"claims\": report}\n    payload = json.dumps(out, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n    if args.json_out:\n        Path(args.json_out).write_text(payload, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(payload)\n    return 0 if not any_fail else 2\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","tool_call_id":"call34f375537fe6429e8ea229603263d536"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"callc96e4486849a4c5fa0c110d57cc3a7d0","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/workspace/inputs/previous_skill/scripts/cvlib.py\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Shared CV PDF extraction helpers for the cv-jd-interview-screening skill.\n\nDesign rules:\n- Explicit errors (missing/empty/corrupt/zero-page PDF) are returned, never\n  fabricated into an empty success.\n- Text is returned per page; candidate identity is anchored by file content\n  (sha256), never by filename conventions.\n- Whitespace normalization is shared with evidence_check.py so literal quotes\n  are matched identically in both tools.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ntry:\n    import pymupdf\nexcept ImportError:  # pragma: no cover\n    pymupdf = None\n\n\nclass ExtractError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised with a precise reason when a PDF cannot be extracted.\"\"\"\n\n\n# A watermark line: a single long alphanumeric token alone on one line,\n# typical of resume-platform trackers. Dropped from cleaned text.\n_WATERMARK_RE = re.compile(r\"^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{24,}$\")\n\n\ndef normalize(text):\n    \"\"\"Collapse all whitespace so quotes match across PDF line breaks.\"\"\"\n    return re.sub(r\"\\s+\", \"\", text)\n\n\ndef clean_page_text(raw):\n    lines = []\n    for line in raw.splitlines():\n        stripped = line.strip()\n        if not stripped:\n            continue\n        if _WATERMARK_RE.match(stripped):\n            continue\n        lines.append(stripped)\n    return lines\n\n\ndef extract_pdf(path):\n    \"\"\"Extract per-page text from one PDF path. Raises ExtractError.\"\"\"\n    if pymupdf is None:\n        raise ExtractError(\"pymupdf not available in this environment\")\n    p = Path(path)\n    if not p.exists():\n        raise ExtractError(f\"file not found: {p}\")\n    try:\n        data = p.read_bytes()\n    except OSError as exc:\n        raise ExtractError(f\"unreadable file: {p}: {exc}\")\n    if len(data) == 0:\n        raise ExtractError(f\"empty file (0 bytes): {p}\")\n    if not data.startswith(b\"%PDF-\"):\n        raise ExtractError(f\"not a PDF (bad header): {p}\")\n    try:\n        doc = pymupdf.open(stream=data, filetype=\"pdf\")\n    except Exception as exc:\n        raise ExtractError(f\"corrupt/unopenable PDF: {p}: {exc}\")\n    if doc.page_count == 0:\n        raise ExtractError(f\"PDF has zero pages: {p}\")\n    pages = []\n    for i, page in enumerate(doc):\n        raw = page.get_text()\n        cleaned = clean_page_text(raw)\n        pages.append({\n            \"page\": i + 1,\n            \"lines\": cleaned,\n            \"text\": \"\\n\".join(cleaned),\n        })\n    doc.close()\n    sha = hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()\n    identity_lines = pages[0][\"lines\"][:6]\n    return {\n        \"file\": str(p),\n        \"candidate_id\": \"cv_\" + sha[:12],\n        \"sha256\": sha,\n        \"bytes\": len(data),\n        \"page_count\": len(pages),\n        \"identity_lines\": identity_lines,\n        \"pages\": pages,\n    }\n\n\ndef extract_many(paths):\n    \"\"\"Extract a batch. Returns (results, errors); candidates never mix\n    because each result carries its own candidate_id and page list.\"\"\"\n    results, errors = [], []\n    for path in paths:\n        try:\n            results.append(extract_pdf(path))\n        except ExtractError as exc:\n            errors.append({\"file\": str(path), \"error\": str(exc)})\n    return results, errors\n\n\ndef find_quote(cv, quote, page=None):\n    \"\"\"Locate a normalized literal quote. Returns dict with ok/reason and the\n    page(s) where the quote actually occurs (for mismatch diagnostics).\"\"\"\n    norm = normalize(quote)\n    if not norm:\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"reason\": \"empty quote\"}\n    hits = [pg[\"page\"] for pg in cv[\"pages\"] if norm in normalize(pg[\"text\"])]\n    if page is not None and (page < 1 or page > cv[\"page_count\"]):\n        return {\n            \"ok\": False,\n            \"reason\": f\"page {page} out of range (1..{cv['page_count']})\",\n            \"found_pages\": hits,\n        }\n    if page is not None:\n        if page in hits:\n            return {\"ok\": True, \"page\": page}\n        return {\"ok\": False, \"reason\": \"quote not on claimed page\", \"found_pages\": hits}\n    if hits:\n        return {\"ok\": True, \"page\": hits[0]}\n    return {\"ok\": False, \"reason\": \"quote not found in document\", \"found_pages\": []}\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(\"cvlib is a library; run cv_extract.py or evidence_check.py\", file=sys.stderr)\n    sys.exit(1)\n","tool_call_id":"callc96e4486849a4c5fa0c110d57cc3a7d0"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call2416f7991505434297fe1c29a6c2d3a9","type":"function","function":{"name":"read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"/workspace/inputs/independent/repair_contract_tests.py\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"from pathlib import Path\nimport json,re,subprocess,sys\nS=Path('/workspace/outputs/skill/scripts')\nF=Path('/workspace/independent_fixtures')\nT=Path('/workspace/extra_type_checks')\nout=Path('/workspace/outputs/independent_retest');out.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\nrows=[]\ndef run(label,*args):\n r=subprocess.run([sys.executable,*map(str,args)],capture_output=True,text=True)\n row={'label':label,'argv':[sys.executable,*map(str,args)],'rc':r.returncode,'stdout':r.stdout,'stderr':r.stderr};rows.append(row)\n try:o=json.loads(r.stdout)\n except ValueError:o=None\n return r,o,row\ndef mark(row,ok,expected):row.update(pass_=bool(ok),expected=expected)\n# Read only diagnostic fields, bound to the same claim. Echoed file/quote/value\n# fields are deliberately excluded. This accepts the original claims report or\n# nested structured errors without requiring one replacement output schema.\ndef claim_index(node,inherited=None):\n for key in ('index','claim_index','item_index'):\n  value=node.get(key)\n  if type(value) is int:return value\n path=node.get('path',node.get('instance_path',node.get('loc')))\n if isinstance(path,list):\n  for value in path:\n   if type(value) is int:return value\n if isinstance(path,str):\n  match=re.search(r'(?:claims?\\s*)?(?:\\[|/|\\.)(\\d+)(?:\\]|/|\\.|$)',path)\n  if match:return int(match.group(1))\n return inherited\ndef diagnostics(report):\n found=[]\n def visit(node,idx=None):\n  if isinstance(node,list):\n   for child in node:visit(child,idx)\n  elif isinstance(node,dict):\n   idx=claim_index(node,idx)\n   words=[]\n   for key in ('reason','error','message','detail','code','type'):\n    value=node.get(key)\n    if isinstance(value,str):words.append(value)\n   # A field/path can identify a diagnostic, but cannot itself prove a type\n   # error; no words are taken from the echoed input file or quote.\n   locations=[]\n   for key in ('field','path','instance_path','loc'):\n    value=node.get(key)\n    if isinstance(value,(str,list)):locations.append(str(value))\n   if words:found.append((idx,' '.join(locations).lower(),' '.join(words).lower()))\n   for key in ('claims','errors','diagnostics','results','error','details'):\n    value=node.get(key)\n    if isinstance(value,(dict,list)):visit(value,idx)\n visit(report)\n return found\ndef typed_diagnostic(report,index,field,kind='type'):\n for idx,location,reason in diagnostics(report):\n  if idx!=index:continue\n  if field=='claim':\n   field_ok=any(x in reason+location for x in ('claim','item','object','mapping','dict','对象'))\n   expected=any(x in reason for x in ('object','mapping','dict','对象